No such certificate is known. The requested map would be a noninjective complex Keller map in dimension \(3\), thereby refuting the open complex Jacobian conjecture. There is no known counterexample of degree \(7\)—or of any degree—for the stated constant-Jacobian condition. Degree-\(6\) Pinchuk-type examples concern the distinct real condition that the Jacobian is nonvanishing but not constant. Declaring a finite extension of \(\mathbb Q\) cannot avoid this, since every such field embeds into \(\mathbb C\).

